course: dictionary
lesson: 14843
title: Raiding: a sudden attack or search
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Raiding means making a sudden attack on a place, usually to steal things or catch people. «The Vikings were raiding the monastery on the coast.» The clues are attack and steal, so raiding is a surprise attack, not a friendly visit.
explain: Police raiding a house means they go in suddenly to search it or to arrest people. «The police were raiding the house at dawn.» The clue is at dawn: it was early, quick and unexpected. Check your meaning by swapping it in: sudden search fits the sentence.
explain: Raiding can be a joke too. «Ben was raiding the biscuit tin when Mum came in.» Ben was not attacking anyone. He was taking biscuits secretly, and the word secretly is the clue to the meaning.
fact: Raiding is the -ing form of the verb raid: raid, raids, raided, raiding.
fact: «Raiding» means making a sudden attack or search, usually to steal something or catch people.
fact: «Raiding parties» were groups sent out to attack, as Vikings did along the coasts of Britain and Ireland.
fact: In games, raiding means attacking an enemy base.
fact: Informal use: raiding the fridge or the biscuit tin means taking food from it, often secretly.
exercise: «The Vikings were raiding the monastery on the coast.» What does raiding mean here? | A slow walk along the beach | A big party with music | A kind visit to say hello | *A sudden attack to steal things
exercise: «The police were raiding the house at dawn.» Why were the police raiding the house? | To paint the walls | To give the family a present | *To go in suddenly and search it | To count the windows
exercise: «Ben was raiding the biscuit tin when Mum came in.» What is Ben doing? | *Taking biscuits from the tin, secretly | Filling the tin with flour | Cleaning the tin | Singing to the tin
test: Which word is the -ing form of raid? | *raiding | raids | raided | raid
test: In a game, what does raiding an enemy base mean? | *Attacking the enemy's base | Sharing snacks with the enemy | Building a house for your team | Sleeping in the base
exam: «The raiding party crept into the town at night.» What is a raiding party? | *A group sent out to attack or steal | A team that cleans the streets | A group of teachers on a school trip | A choir singing at night
